a/covert-cafe-ncb-busts-secret-basement-meow-meow-lab-in-ahmedabad/articleshow/135894404.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/covert-cafe-ncb-busts-secret-basement-meow-meow-lab-in-ahmedabad/articleshow/135894404.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-16T21:02:15+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Raj Shekhar Jha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135894519,imgsize-171272.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Census 2027: Self-enumeration begins in four states, house-to-house count from December 1]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/census-2027-self-enumeration-begins-in-four-states-house-to-house-count-from-december-1/articleshow/135892756.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135892756.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[The Census 2027 self-enumeration process has commenced in Uttar Pradesh, Punjab, Goa, and Uttarakhand, running until November 30. Following this, house-to-house enumeration will begin on December 1. The initiative aims to gather a range of data, including caste details from respondents, with an open-ended approach. Meanwhile, Manipur's census has been postponed due to local concerns regarding the national register of citizens.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/census-2027-self-enumeration-begins-in-four-states-house-to-house-count-from-december-1/articleshow/135892756.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/census-2027-self-enumeration-begins-in-four-states-house-to-house-count-from-december-1/articleshow/135892756.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-16T20:06:53+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Bharti Jain</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135893003,imgsize-175758.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[IISc researchers find antibiotic combination to reverse drug resistance in TB]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/iisc-researchers-find-antibiotic-combination-to-reverse-drug-resistance-in-tb/articleshow/135892833.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135892833.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/iisc-researchers-find-antibiotic-combination-to-reverse-drug-resistance-in-tb/articleshow/135892833.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/iisc-researchers-find-antibiotic-combination-to-reverse-drug-resistance-in-tb/articleshow/135892833.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-16T20:03:53+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Chethan Kumar</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135892939,imgsize-95402.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['I felt accepted': Sonia Gandhi revisits 2004 Cong win, opens up at memoir launch]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/i-felt-accepted-sonia-gandhi-revisits-2004-cong-win-opens-up-at-memoir-launch/articleshow/135892803.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135892803.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Sonia Gandhi's memoir release shed light on her journey of acceptance in India post the 2004 Congress victory. She shared her early experiences with Indira Gandhi, detailing feelings of both intimidation and admiration over time. Following the tragic assassination of Rajiv Gandhi, her children emerged as pillars of emotional strength. Sonia's message to the youth emphasizes the importance of participating in politics and civic life.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://tim